From: naelolaiz <1333555+naelolaiz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:34:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] main/e2fsprogs: build without fuse2fs when
 bootstrapping

With BOOTSTRAP or APORTS_BOOTSTRAP set, leave out fuse3-dev and the
fuse2fs subpackages. fuse3 pulls in eudev, glib, gobject-introspection
and cairo, about 90 source packages on a new architecture. configure
builds fuse2fs only when it finds fuse, so nothing else changes; the
rest of e2fsprogs (mke2fs, e2fsck, the libraries mc links for ext2
attributes) builds as before.

Without the variables the APKBUILD builds exactly what it built before.
Generic, not specific to riscv32.
---
 main/e2fsprogs/APKBUILD | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/main/e2fsprogs/APKBUILD b/main/e2fsprogs/APKBUILD
index 543229bb5e4..7e825813d93 100644
--- a/main/e2fsprogs/APKBUILD
+++ b/main/e2fsprogs/APKBUILD
@@ -8,14 +8,20 @@ url="https://e2fsprogs.sourceforge.net/"
 arch="all"
 license="GPL-2.0-or-later AND LGPL-2.0-or-later AND BSD-3-Clause AND MIT"
 depends_dev="util-linux-dev gawk"
-makedepends="$depends_dev linux-headers fuse3-dev"
+makedepends="$depends_dev linux-headers"
 checkdepends="diffutils perl coreutils"
 subpackages="
 	$pkgname-static
 	$pkgname-dev
 	libcom_err
-	fuse2fs
-	fuse2fs-doc:fuse2fs_doc:noarch
+	"
+if [ -z "$BOOTSTRAP" ] && [ -z "$APORTS_BOOTSTRAP" ]; then
+	# fuse3 pulls in eudev, glib and gobject-introspection;
+	# configure builds fuse2fs only when it finds fuse
+	makedepends="$makedepends fuse3-dev"
+	subpackages="$subpackages fuse2fs fuse2fs-doc:fuse2fs_doc:noarch"
+fi
+subpackages="$subpackages
 	$pkgname-doc
 	$pkgname-libs
 	$pkgname-extra
